9697-library-new-request-tools.jackson.module-jackson-module-blackbird-3.1.5-9e485768\n\nThe likely blocker is the dynamic-access coverage target, not the final Gradle/native test. After 6 iterations, coverage remained at 8/9 (88.89%). The sole uncovered call is `Constructor.newInstance(...)` in `ReflectionHack$Java8.lambda$privateLookupIn$0` at `ReflectionHack.java:84`. The generation log concludes that this Java 8 fallback cannot be reached through supported behavior because version 3.1.5 targets Java 17 and selects `Java9Up.FACTORY`; forcing it would require unsupported Java 8 or private-state manipulation. Meanwhile, the latest full test run passed all 7 JVM/native tests. An earlier run also exposed a potentially flaky concurrent serializer test with `Concurrent serializer executor did not terminate`, although subsequent runs passed.\n\nInspect:\n- `logs/tools.jackson.module:jackson-module-blackbird:3.1.5/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-02T15-21-30-566779Z.log`\n- `logs/tools.jackson.module:jackson-module-blackbird:3.1.5/gradle/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-02T16-10-05-096322Z.log`\n- `logs/tools.jackson.module:jackson-module-blackbird:3.1.5/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-02T16-08-56-719282Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Review whether the unreachable Java 8-only call site can be accepted as exhausted at 8/9 coverage.\n2. Stress-test or simplify `CrossLoaderAccessTest` to rule out the observed executor-termination flake.\n3. Run the coordinate-scoped metadata validation and full test lanes across the required environments, then finalize the preserved work if they pass.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0a8b8f4600699bfa016a984b62394887d2aa4ca969b5d7c24e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 5035, "output": 989, "cacheRead": 133888, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 139912, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cach